{"id":"huldah","name":"Huldah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:huldah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Huldah","text":"Weasel, a prophetess; the wife of Shallum. She was consulted regarding the “book of the law” discovered by the high priest Hilkiah (2 Kings 22:14-20; 2 Chr. 34:22-28). She resided in that part of Jerusalem called the Mishneh (A.V., “the college;” R.V., “the second quarter”), supposed by some to be the suburb between the inner and the outer wall, the second or lower city, Akra. Miriam (Ex. 15:20) and Deborah (Judg. 4:4) are the only others who bear the title of “prophetess,” for the word in Isa. 8:3 means only the prophet’s wife."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H4725","lemma":"מָקוֹם","xlit":"mâqôwm","gloss":"a standing","kjv":"country, home, open, place","count":8,"share":0.57},{"strong":"H899","lemma":"בֶּגֶד","xlit":"beged","gloss":"a covering","kjv":"apparel, cloth, garment, lap","count":4,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H3427","lemma":"יָשַׁב","xlit":"yâshab","gloss":"to sit down","kjv":"abide, continue, dwell, ease self","count":7,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H1697","lemma":"דָּבָר","xlit":"dâbâr","gloss":"a word","kjv":"act, advice, affair, answer","count":6,"share":0.43},{"strong":"H7451","lemma":"רַע","xlit":"raʻ","gloss":"bad or evil","kjv":"adversity, affliction, bad, calamity","count":4,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H4428","lemma":"מֶלֶךְ","xlit":"melek","gloss":"a king","kjv":"king, royal","count":7,"share":0.5}],"verses":["2Kgs.22.16","2Kgs.22.17","2Kgs.22.19","2Kgs.22.20","2Chr.34.24","2Chr.34.25","2Chr.34.27","2Chr.34.28","2Kgs.22.14","2Kgs.22.15","2Kgs.22.18","2Chr.34.22","2Chr.34.23","2Chr.34.26"],"related":[{"id":"asahiah","type":"cooccur","shared":14,"jaccard":0.778,"why":"14 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"josiah","type":"cooccur","shared":14,"jaccard":0.135,"why":"14 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"women","type":"cooccur","shared":14,"jaccard":0.016,"why":"14 verses are indexed under both"},{"id